# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything except the documented template. Getting this right in the first
# commit matters more than it looks: an API key in git history is not something
# you want to find on a repo you're linking from a portfolio.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm/
*.tgz

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Tooling caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.turbo/
.vite/
.cache/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ── Runtime scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploaded documents while running locally; the real ones live in object storage.
uploads/
tmp/

# ── Local database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pgdata/

# ── Subagent-driven-development scratch ──────────────────────────────────────
# Ledgers, briefs, and review packages for in-progress plan execution.
.superpowers/

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
